<title>BANGLADESH: Defence tops Bangladesh 1997/98 revenue allocation.</title>
<headline>Defence tops Bangladesh 1997/98 revenue allocation.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Defence received the highest allocation in Bangladesh's 1997/98 budget (July-June) proposed in the parliament on Thursday.</p>
<p>Finance Minister S.A.M.S. Kibria proposed to raise the allocation for defence sector by 1.92 billion taka to 24.57 billion taka in 1997/98.</p>
<p>The sector was allocated 16.89 percent of the projected 145.44 billion taka 1997/98 revenue spendings.</p>
<p>Education closely follows defence with 23.42 billion taka.</p>
<p>($1=43.75 taka)</p>
</text>
